  "content": {
    "id": "p21-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "The value of a brand new car is $\\$25,000$. It depreciates at a rate of 10% per year.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p21-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the value of the car after 1 year.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$22,500$",
          "worked": "The car retains $100\\%-10\\%=90\\%$ of its value each year.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}V(1)&=25\\,000(0.9)\\\\V(1)&=22\\,500\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe car is worth $\\$22,500$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find the value of the car after 2 years.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\$20,250$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}V(2)&=22\\,500(0.9)\\\\V(2)&=20\\,250\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe car is worth $\\$20,250$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Make a formula that models the value of the car after $n$ years.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$V(n)=25\\,000(0.9)^n$ dollars",
          "worked": "The initial value is $\\$25,000$. Multiply by $0.9$ once for each of the $n$ years.\n\n$$V(n)=25\\,000(0.9)^n$$\n\nHere $V(n)$ is the value in dollars.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 11
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "What percentage of the original price is the value of the car after 5 years? Give your answer to the nearest whole percent.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$59\\%$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{V(5)}{V(0)}\\times 100\\%&=\\frac{25\\,000(0.9)^5}{25\\,000}\\times 100\\%\\\\\\frac{V(5)}{V(0)}\\times 100\\%&=59.049\\%\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis rounds to $59\\%$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 14
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "During which year will the value of the car drop below $\\$10,000$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The 9th year.",
          "worked": "Let $t$ be the elapsed time in years. At the threshold,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}25\\,000(0.9)^t&=10\\,000\\\\(0.9)^t&=0.4\\\\t\\ln(0.9)&=\\ln(0.4)\\\\t&=\\frac{\\ln(0.4)}{\\ln(0.9)}\\\\t&\\approx 8.70.\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe value decreases, so it drops below $\\$10,000$ between 8 and 9 years, during the 9th year.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
